# Helvety Cloud constitution

Before feature work, read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/architecture/ROADMAP.md`. Implement **one scoped change per chat**.

## Must

- Zero knowledge: Helvety cannot decrypt your data. No master key, escrow, or support content recovery.
- No account passwords. Supabase Auth: email OTP only. Encryption unlock: WebAuthn PRF (session ≠ decrypt).
- Greenfield only in `helvety-cloud`. Never copy from `helvety` or `helvety-browser-extension-chromium`.
- Prefer free-tier infra: Supabase Free, Vercel Hobby. Stripe is allowed for customer billing. Omit Redis, Sentry, paid CI, analytics, etc.
- Encrypted entity I/O via `/api/v1` + Bearer JWT. Browser may use Supabase Auth SDK; must not use PostgREST for encrypted entity tables.
- Supabase project `qnoeiurmyyyuawkcifmw` (helvety-cloud, Zurich) only, never `bkdzeihxzvrkndjvyzye`.
- Prefer Supabase/Vercel MCP and schema-as-code (`docs/architecture/SCHEMA_WORKFLOW.md`).
- No misleading E2EE/recovery claims in UI or docs (`docs/architecture/LEGAL_REQUIREMENTS.md`).

## Must not

- Invent multi-phase roadmaps or ship many unrelated changes in one chat unless the user explicitly expands scope.
- Add paid SaaS “for best practice” (Stripe for customer billing is fine).
- Public signup/billing without the live legal pack and acceptance gates (P-legal2). Counsel review is optional for risk, not a product gate.
